      "content": "## Nexus-7 Proximity Sensor Quick-Start Guide\n\n**1. Sensor Overview and Specifications**\nThe Nexus-7 is an I2C proximity sensor designed for reliable short- to long-range detection. Key specifications include a operating voltage range of 3.3V to 5.0V DC and an effective range spanning 2cm up to 400cm.\n\n**2. Physical Installation and Wiring**\nSecure the sensor onto the desired chassis using the integrated M3 screw holes. For electrical setup, connect the sensor using the 4-pin header: VCC, GND, SDA, and SCL to your micro-controller.\n\n**3. Software Configuration Guide**\nOnce physically mounted and connected, ensure your host system assigns the correct I2C address, which is fixed at 0x29. This final step enables proper communication with the sensor.\n\n**4. Critical Operation Safety Notices**\nIt is crucial to adhere to these warnings to prevent damage. Under no circumstances should the applied voltage exceed 5.5V, as this will permanently damage the sensor circuitry; furthermore, standard ESD precautions must be observed during handling.",
